From 888703467e0d91a67874f35b2a9f300abe2c3d11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:11:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] linkbus: snapshot SAB multiboard backend for a
 deterministic master pair

The SAB multiboard backend shares the 1 MB bank and the status word
live between the master and its graphics partner, so what a board reads
between two sync points depends on host timing. In the single-page
cabinet this made board 0's state differ between runs.

makeSabSnapshotMultiboardBackend (exported as
linkbus_install_sab_multiboard_snapshot) keeps a private copy of the
bank and the status word on each board and logs its writes (one entry
per word, newest value; status ops in order). At each sync point it
publishes its log, passes a generation barrier, applies the logs of all
boards in the barrier in board id order to its own copy, then passes a
second barrier before the next log can be written. All copies are equal
after every sync. Board 0 also applies the logs to the shared bank, from
which a partner takes its first copy (the master cannot pass a barrier
before the partner arrives, so the copy is stable). Writes reach the
other board at the next sync point instead of at once. Layout:
MultiboardSnapshotLayout (live layout plus one log region per board).
linkbus_sab_snapshot_stats reports syncs, log overflows, second barrier
timeouts and a bank hash. The live backend is unchanged.

CMake: LINKBUS_MULTIBOARD now defaults to ON (Emscripten only), so the
unchanged build-win.ps1 builds the multiboard class. Side effect: the
f355 and sgdrvsim table entries (gated by NAOMI_MULTIBOARD) are now in
the browser build.

linkbus_ring_stats exports the eight ring counters.

